{"filePath": ".tmp-rel26.json", "content": "{
  "tag_name": "v1.10.26-qa",
  "name": "IVX Holdings v1.10.26 — the Home black screen was a missing line",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": false,
  "body": "## The Home black screen: one missing line\n\n`app/(tabs)/_layout.tsx` — the real defect:\n\n```js\nconst TABS_LOADING_TIMEOUT_MS = 2000;\n\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!isLoading) {\n    setLoadingTimedOut(false);\n    // setAuthInitError(null)  <-- THIS LINE DID NOT EXIST\n    return;\n  }\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => {\n    setLoadingTimedOut(true);\n    setAuthInitError('IVX startup took too long...');\n  }, TABS_LOADING_TIMEOUT_MS);\n  return () => clearTimeout(timer);\n}, [isLoading]);\n```\n\nWhen auth finished, the code reset `loadingTimedOut` but **never cleared `authInitError`**. And the `if (authInitError)` branch returns **before** `<Tabs>` is ever rendered.\n\nSo a single launch slower than 2 seconds — routine on mobile data, where the Supabase session call regularly exceeds two seconds — permanently replaced the entire tab tree, **Home included, for the whole session**. Auth succeeding did not bring Home back. Navigating did not bring Home back. Nothing threw, so no error boundary, no crash log, and no error screen ever reported it.\n\n**Fixed:** the missing `setAuthInitError(null)`, plus the timeout raised 2000ms -> 12000ms because 2 seconds was never a realistic budget for a real device on a real network.\n\n## One of the black screens was my own diagnostic\n\n`BlankScreenWatchdog` mounted a full-screen **opaque** layer directly above the entire app:\n\n```js\noverlay: {\n  ...StyleSheet.absoluteFillObject,\n  backgroundColor: '#0A0A0F',\n  zIndex: 9999,\n}\n```\n\n`#0A0A0F` is `rgb(10,10,15)`. The device recording measured `rgb(12,8,14)`.\n\nIt never caught a single real defect. It falsely accused working screens twice, and its own recovery button navigated into a route that rendered nothing. A diagnostic that can paint the whole screen near-black is not a safety net — it is another way to get a black screen. **Deleted.**\n\n## Why this kept coming back\n\nFour different waiting states all used the identical near-black `#0A0A0F`: root startup, routing, sign-in, and that overlay. A screenshot of a stuck app could not distinguish them, so every diagnosis was a guess.\n\nEach stage now owns a distinct colour and prints its own name:\n\n- **STAGE 1 - STARTING** — `#0A0A0F` (root startup)\n- **STAGE 2 · ROUTING** — `#0B1220` navy (route `/`)\n- **STAGE 3 · SIGNING IN** — `#141007` warm dark (tabs auth)\n\nOne screenshot now names the exact stage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- Routing + crash-shield suites: **46 pass / 0 fail**\n- Full suite: **1192 pass**, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures (unchanged)\n- Gradle: **BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 1m 38s**\n\n### Verified inside the shipped bundle\n\nThe overlay strings are **absent**, confirming the removal:\n\n```\nScreen failed to load    ascii=-1 utf16=-1  -> GONE\nGo to Home               ascii=-1 utf16=-1  -> GONE\nBack to Login            ascii=-1 utf16=-1  -> GONE\nblank-screen-watchdog    ascii=-1 utf16=-1  -> GONE\n```\n\nThe new stage labels are **present** (the `·` ones live in Hermes' UTF-16 string table, so an ASCII grep alone would wrongly report them missing):\n\n```\nSTAGE 1 - STARTING       ascii   offset=1791555\nSTAGE 2 · ROUTING        utf16   offset=3392230\nSTAGE 3 · SIGNING IN     utf16   offset=3424632\n```\n\nStamp `1.10.26 (124)`; `(tabs)/(home)` still absent; `IVX Runtime Error`, `Previous Crash Detected`, `IVX Render Error`, `invalid_credentials`, `IVX startup timed out`, `index-route` all retained.\n\nversionName 1.10.26 / versionCode 124\nSHA256: `f64e5774935deca02f66d26b8e84ab6c82237f1ba1b53b7b879615f9ac8d13c1`"
}
